          "id": "9c5bfdc4-728f-4917-9a4e-80d8bd4d6144",
          "name": "Debit cash from an account.",
          "request": {
            "name": "Debit cash from an account.",
            "description": {
              "content": "The Phase 1 measured write path. Which implementation runs is chosen\nper request:\n\n- `x-daftar-naive-overdraft: true` — application funds check, then an\n  atomic `balance = balance - $1`. Produces **overdrafts** and\n  **zero lost updates**: the self-referential UPDATE is re-evaluated\n  against the committed row version under READ COMMITTED, so the final\n  balance is arithmetically exact, just negative.\n- `x-daftar-naive-lost-update: true` — read, compute in application code,\n  write an absolute value. **Loses updates**, so the final balance is\n  higher than it should be and money is created from nothing.\n- neither — a single guarded statement\n  (`... WHERE balance >= $1`). Correct.\n\nBoth naive paths are permanent, documented deliverables.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/accounts/:externalId/debits",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "accounts",
                ":externalId",
                "debits"
              ],
              "query": [],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "cash-0001",
                  "key": "externalId",
                  "description": "(Required) Opaque client-facing account identifier."
